[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) is marked known: one issue, one fix queued. Its reports say otherwise.
Read by what each report describes, and placed by the tenant's locale and booking form (the rules
in `causes.ts`), #4471 holds more than one problem. The fix queued for the parser closes one of them.

<Callout kind="warn">
Not one issue. Each problem below has its own ticket, its own fix and its own count.
</Callout>

## What #4471 holds

<ProblemTable ticket={4471} />

## The problems

### `parser`: the month comes first

The shared parser reads every date month first. Every tenant in #4471 writes the day first, so any
date with a day of 12 or less comes out with day and month swapped: 7 April becomes 4 July. This is
the problem #4471 was opened for, and the queued fix is for this one.

<ProblemReports ticket={4471} problem="parser" />

### `hint`: the form tells people the wrong order

Tenants on `booking-v3` show `MM/DD/YYYY` under the date field. People type what the hint says,
month first, and the form reads it the tenant's way, day first. The result is the same swap, but the
parser fix does not touch it: these reports come only through the form, only on `booking-v3`. Intake
tags reports by the reporter's browser, so its `hint` tag misses some of these and lands on others
that are not.

<ProblemReports ticket={4471} problem="hint" />

### `day-move`: one day off, not a month

These reports describe no swap. A booking moves by one day, an invite arrives before the booking
was made, two clients in different time zones get different days for the same meeting, every June
booking is off by a day. That is a time zone or day boundary problem, not date order. The desk already
noted them (`desk-notes.json`) and the old table still counts them under `parser`. The parser fix
will not close them.

<ProblemReports ticket={4471} problem="day-move" />

## Why one ticket hid three

Reports are merged on subject alone ([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject)).
Subjects like "Date is wrong" fit every problem here, so all of them landed in #4471. The old
table, for comparison:

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

## For the desk

- Before you mark a big ticket known, place its reports by cause, not by subject.
- A report that does not fit the cause gets its own ticket, not a footnote.

